From: Carl Andersson <carl.andersson@dynamist.se>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/fs: retry an open without O_NOATIME on EPERM

overlayfs opens its lower files with O_NOATIME. do_open keeps the flag
when the process holds CAP_FOWNER, but inside a user namespace that
capability covers only files whose owner is mapped into the namespace.
A host store owned by the unmapped root then fails every open with
EPERM, and the guest's first exec from its /nix overlay fails with
"Operation not permitted".

This retries such an open without O_NOATIME, and that is all the flag
costs: an atime update on a read-only store does nothing. virtiofsd
serves the same store in the same namespace without the failure.
---
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/linux/passthrough.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/linux/passthrough.rs
@@ -699,7 +699,18 @@
             } else {
                 None
             };
-            RwLock::new(self.open_inode(inode, flags as i32)?)
+            // CAP_FOWNER in a user namespace covers only files whose owner
+            // is mapped into it, so O_NOATIME can still fail with EPERM.
+            let file = match self.open_inode(inode, flags as i32) {
+                Err(e)
+                    if e.raw_os_error() == Some(libc::EPERM)
+                        && flags & (libc::O_NOATIME as u32) != 0 =>
+                {
+                    self.open_inode(inode, (flags & !(libc::O_NOATIME as u32)) as i32)?
+                }
+                result => result?,
+            };
+            RwLock::new(file)
         };
 
         let handle = self.next_handle.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
